\subsection{Phase F: localized stochastic stability in the source funnel}
\label{sec:stability-widening-phase-f}

The stochastic qualification uses the same source-word Lyapunov function $W_i$
and the same certified word family as the deterministic result.  It does not
introduce a separate Euclidean $N$-step contraction or a second nonlinear tube.
Because exact Gaussian increments have unbounded support, the proof first
constructs a mean-square drift result for a localized noise process that remains
inside the certified funnel and then bounds the finite-horizon probability that
the true Gaussian process differs from that localized process.

Fix a source word $w:i\to j$ of length at most $\ell_+$.  Let
$\mathcal F_w(e,0)$ be its exact branch-fixed zero-noise map and let
$\lambda_w<1$ be its certified funnel factor.  Define
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \lambda_W:=\max_{m,w}\lambda_w<1.}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-margin}
\end{equation}
The maximization is over the source-complete word families in the fixed-
dimensional normal-Live modes.  Dimension-changing jumps are handled by their
certified funnel inequalities before the next same-mode stochastic word.

Choose a physical-sample noise radius $w_*>0$ for which every source-word prefix
starting in the selected stochastic funnel remains inside its certified domain
whenever $\|w_k\|\le w_*$.  Define radial localization
\begin{equation}
 \vct w_k^{\,c}:=
 \begin{cases}
 \vct w_k,&\|\vct w_k\|\le w_*,\\
 w_*\vct w_k/\|\vct w_k\|,&\|\vct w_k\|>w_*.
 \end{cases}
 \label{eq:widen-gaussian-noise}
\end{equation}
The localized and exact trajectories coincide until the first raw increment
whose norm exceeds $w_*$.  Localization and NIS branch selection can destroy
conditional zero mean; no zero-mean cancellation is used below.

The active error lives on a product of the attitude group and additive error
coordinates.  For source node $j$ define the product distance
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 d_{\mathcal X,j}^2
 \bigl((\mat R_1,\vct\xi_1),(\mat R_2,\vct\xi_2)\bigr)
 :=d_{\SO(3)}(\mat R_1,\mat R_2)^2
   +\|\vct\xi_1-\vct\xi_2\|^2.}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-product-distance}
\end{equation}
Any fixed source scaling may be included in the additive norm; on the compact
proof domain it changes only the finite equivalence constants.

For a realized source word define the exact noisy-to-zero-noise endpoint
separation
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \Delta_w^c:=d_{\mathcal X,j}\!\left(
 \mathcal F_w(e,w^c),\mathcal F_w(e,0)\right).}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-remainder}
\end{equation}
This definition never subtracts two attitudes.  On the compact source funnel,
smoothness of the exact prediction, correction, quaternion reset, covariance
recursion, and accepted branch maps gives a finite one-step incremental bound
of the form
\begin{equation}
 \delta_{k+1}
 \le L_{\mathcal X}\delta_k
 +(\bar G+c_{zw}r_*)\|w_k^c\|
 +c_{ww}\|w_k^c\|^2,
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-one-step-noise}
\end{equation}
where $\delta_k$ is the product distance between the branch-matched noisy and
zero-noise trajectories, $r_*$ is a fixed norm-equivalent size of the compact
funnel, and all constants are uniform over the certified source family.

Assume the raw pre-gate increments obey the conditional moment bounds
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E[\|w_k\|^2\mid\mathscr F_k]\le s_2,
 \qquad
 \mathbb E[\|w_k\|^4\mid\mathscr F_k]\le s_4.
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-moments}
\end{equation}
For conditionally Gaussian pre-gate noise with
$\Sigma_k\preceq\overline\Sigma$, one may take
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 s_2=\operatorname{tr}\overline\Sigma,
 \qquad
 s_4=s_2^2+2\operatorname{tr}(\overline\Sigma^2).}
 \label{eq:widen-gaussian-moments}
\end{equation}
Radial localization can only reduce the noise norm, so the same moment bounds
hold for $w_k^c$.

Let $g_*:=\bar G+c_{zw}r_*$ and define
\begin{align}
 \nu_1&:=2g_*^2s_2+2c_{ww}^2s_4,\\
 \boxed{
 \nu_W:=\ell_+\nu_1
 \sum_{r=0}^{\ell_+-1}L_{\mathcal X}^{2r}.}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-floor}
\end{align}
Starting from zero branch-matched separation at the word entrance, repeated use
of Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-stochastic-one-step-noise} and Cauchy--Schwarz gives, for
every realized certified word,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb E[(\Delta_w^c)^2\mid\mathscr F_n]\le\nu_W.}
 \label{eq:widen-lifted-noise-moment}
\end{equation}
No independence between physical samples within the word is required.

Because $W_j$ is smooth and positive definite with respect to the adopted gauge
on the compact geodesic funnel, its Riemannian gradient and Hessian have uniform
bounds relative to $W_j$.  On a certified compact geodesic enlargement that
contains the minimizing product geodesic between the branch-matched endpoints,
there are finite constants $g_W,h_W$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_j(y)
 \le W_j(x)
 +g_W\sqrt{W_j(x)}\,d_{\mathcal X,j}(x,y)
 +h_Wd_{\mathcal X,j}(x,y)^2.}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-W-lipschitz}
\end{equation}
This is a second-order bound on the same group/path energy; it does not replace
attitude by an additive coordinate.

\begin{theorem}[Constructive source-word mean-square drift for localized gated noise]
\label{thm:widen-stochastic-drift}
Assume Eqs.~\eqref{eq:widen-stochastic-margin}--
\eqref{eq:widen-stochastic-W-lipschitz}.  At certified word boundaries let
$W_n$ denote the node funnel energy.  Define
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \lambda_s:=\frac{1+\lambda_W}{2}<1,}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-coefficients}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \sigma_s^2:=
 \left(
 h_W+\frac{g_W^2\lambda_W}{2(1-\lambda_W)}
 \right)\nu_W.}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-floor-W}
\end{equation}
Then the localized exact source recursion satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb E[W_{n+1}\mid\mathscr F_n]
 \le\lambda_sW_n+\sigma_s^2.}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-drift}
\end{equation}
Consequently Theorem~\ref{thm:capture-stochastic-live} applies directly to the
same stochastic funnel metric.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
For the realized source word set
$x=\mathcal F_w(e,0)$ and $y=\mathcal F_w(e,w^c)$.  The deterministic funnel
certificate gives $W_j(x)\le\lambda_WW_i(e)$.  Apply
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-stochastic-W-lipschitz}; then conditional
Cauchy--Schwarz and Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-lifted-noise-moment} give
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E[W_j(y)\mid\mathscr F_n]
 \le\lambda_WW_n
 +g_W\sqrt{\lambda_WW_n}\sqrt{\nu_W}
 +h_W\nu_W.
\end{equation}
Young's inequality bounds the middle term by
$(1-\lambda_W)W_n/2+
 g_W^2\lambda_W\nu_W/[2(1-\lambda_W)]$, which yields the stated
$(\lambda_s,\sigma_s^2)$.  The realized branch may depend on within-word
localized noise; no branch-conditioned zero-mean cancellation is needed because
the deterministic funnel inequality and the product-distance sensitivity bound
hold uniformly for every admissible branch.
\end{proof}

For the true unbounded process define the tail event over $K$ word blocks
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal E_K^c:=
 \left\{\max_{0\le r<K}\max_{0\le q<\ell_+}
 \|w_{k_r+q}\|>w_*\right\}.
\end{equation}
A union bound followed by Markov's inequality and the raw moment bounds gives
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \Pr(\mathcal E_K^c)
 \le K\ell_+\min\!\left\{
 \frac{s_2}{w_*^2},\frac{s_4}{w_*^4}\right\}.}
 \label{eq:widen-stochastic-exit}
\end{equation}
On $\mathcal E_K$ the raw and localized trajectories coincide over the complete
horizon, so the true process inherits the same certified regional path and
word-boundary comparison over that horizon.  A Gaussian quadratic-form tail may
replace Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-stochastic-exit} when the sharper probabilistic
certificate of the next stage is constructed.

\begin{remark}[Scope of the stochastic result]
\label{rem:widen-stochastic-scope}
The stochastic certificate uses the same $W_i$, source graph, word family, and
geodesic funnel as the deterministic theory and does not assume that innovation
gating preserves zero conditional mean.  It does not turn the regional MEKF
into a global Gaussian system.  With unbounded Gaussian noise the rigorous claim
remains finite-horizon and high-probability unless additional global recovery
bounds are proved.
\end{remark}
